
# The plugin conformance corpus — SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# plugin.json beside this file is a COMMITTED build artifact compiled from
# here by tools/build-spec.js (@voxgig/model). Every port's test runner
# reads that JSON directly, so no port needs a Node toolchain to run its
# tests. Edit this file, run `npm run build-spec` in tools/, and commit
# both. Never hand-edit the JSON (§16, prime directive 5).
#
# THIS CORPUS IS EMPTY, AND THAT IS P0's EXIT CRITERION.
#
# P0 builds the machinery and proves it turns over: `make spec` compiles
# this file and `make spec-check` proves the committed JSON matches it.
# Both must work before there is anything to compile, because a corpus
# pipeline first exercised on real data is one whose failures arrive mixed
# up with the data's.
#
# P1 fills it in, and the order is an obligation rather than a preference
# (see station's station-and-plugin-plan.md §3):
#
#   C1, owed BEFORE station's Stage 2 — earlier than P1's own exit:
#     ref      name/tag grammar, parse, format, canonicalization,
#              auto-tag, `pos` vs `seq` across a redeclaration
#     config   document normalization, array/map forms, the `default`
#              map, the ten-level precedence ladder, profile overlay,
#              defaults-after-merge, shape-declared merge depth,
#              list-replace
#
#   C2, owed before P1's exit, together with the draft driver contract in
#   DOCS.md (§15.2 — probes, command vocabulary, canonical observable),
#   because these two are DRIVER sections and a port cannot run them from
#   corpus files alone:
#     lifecycle  the state machine, idempotence, illegal transitions,
#                failure paths
#     order      topological sort, bands, ties, vacuous constraints,
#                recomputation
#
# The remaining sections (§15.3) land with the phase that implements them:
# env, resolve, capability, version, graph, declare, nest, state,
# resource, point, export, depend, apply, error, trace.
#
# Adding a section here is not enough on its own — §15.3's table records
# whether it is pure data or driver-based, and a driver section without
# its contract in DOCS.md is a suite no port but this one can implement.


# Spec format version. Version 1 turns on strict entry validation in every
# runner: unknown fields, multiple argument sources, `err` beside `out`,
# and empty sets all fail rather than passing silently.
PLUGIN: version: 1
